		("QUEUE-015", "removing a queue cell removes every cell behind it, where tp.exe has no per-cell removal: the cell clear 0x5367a0 removes one cell and the bulldozer's rectangle pass 0x52bdd0 clears only path cells (type test 0x536310), but the queue tool's undo (0x52fe50: it pops the last point of the tool's stack of corner points, 0x81b738, and lays the line again up to the previous point through 0x524960) shortens a queue by whole segments, and a ride's demolition (0x527ee0) fills that stack from the ride's queue (0x530120, from the entrance cell +0x36 along the link bytes, one point per corner) and undoes every point, refunding the cells (evidence needed: none; OpenTPW's removal from a clicked cell on is its own queue editing)"),
